  "query_preview": "(Friday through Monday)...\nHigh pressure will strengthen into the weekend. The heat is\ncurrently forecast to peak on Saturday with high temperatures 5 to\n10 degrees above average for coastal areas and 10 to 15 degrees\nabove average for inland areas. High temperatures on Saturday will\nrange from around 80 near the coast to 100 to 110 for the Inland\nEmpire with 118 to 122 for the lower deserts. The most likely\nlocations to tie or set new record high temperatures on Saturday\nare in the mountains and lower deserts, though there are some\nadditional valley and inland coastal locations that could also be\nnear record levels.\n\nHigh temperatures will begin to cool a few degrees for Sunday and\nMonday, but still be around 10 degrees above average for inland\nareas on Monday with extreme HeatRisk for the deserts.",
